title: Dashboard › Headline › What the headline and sub line say
route: /dashboard
intro: The big sentence at the top and the muted line under it are rebuilt whenever a filter, a tile or a payer reply changes the list. Stage wins over Payer, and Payer wins over the plain count. The numbers below are the demo's opening data.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A filter, a tile click or a payer reply changes the list"
process p1 "Headline is rebuilt\nCounts use Payer, Program and Request type, but not Stage"
decision d1 "Does any request match the filters?"
screen n0 "'No requests match these filters.'\n'The filters hide everything. Clear them to see every request again.'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Clear filters and empty states"

decision d2 "Which Stage is set?"
screen a1 "Appeal or call\n'7 denials are on their route. $62.4K is at stake.'\n'Each one is a call, an appeal, an external review or a resubmission.'"
screen a2 "Info requested\n'3 requests are waiting on you.'\n'The payer asked for more information. Packet drafts each answer for you to review.'"
screen a3 "Preparing\n'5 requests are being prepared.'\nThe count is the same as the Preparing tile: the table rows plus cases saved in New case\n'They are in Case Manager. Nothing has been sent to a payer yet.'"
screen a4 "Received\n'4 requests have been received.'\n'The payer confirmed receipt. Navigator checks each one again every few minutes.'"
screen a5 "Under review\n'14 requests are under review.'\n'Payers usually take about 2.2 days to decide. Caller phones when one runs late.'"
screen a6 "Decided today\n'8 requests were decided today. 6 approved, 2 not as asked.'\n'Approvals update the ledger. Write-back to the EMR waits for you.'"

decision d3 "Is a Payer set?"
screen b1 "'Cardinal Health Plan: 5 waiting, taking 2.8 days.'\n'Decisions usually take 2 days at this payer. 3 denials are open.'\nWith Program or Type set, they lead the sub line: 'IOP. Decisions usually...'"
decision d4 "Is Program or Request type set?"
screen c1 "'7 requests are waiting on payers. 1 is waiting on you.'\n'Showing Residential 3.5 only. Everything below follows that filter.'"
screen c2 "'18 requests are waiting on payers. 3 are waiting on you.'\n'Where every request stands, from preparing to decided, without a phone call.'"
process p2 "Payer, Program and Request type set are added in front of the sub line\nExample: 'Summit Medicaid HMO. Payers usually take about 1.4 days...'"
end e1 "Headline and sub line shown"

s1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| n0 --> g1
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Appeal or call| a1
d2 -->|Info requested| a2
d2 -->|Preparing| a3
d2 -->|Received| a4
d2 -->|Under review| a5
d2 -->|Decided today| a6
d2 -->|All stages| d3
a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5 & a6 --> p2 --> e1
d3 -->|Yes| b1 --> e1
d3 -->|No| d4
d4 -->|Yes| c1 --> e1
d4 -->|No| c2 --> e1
